# shir_nodes/walk_dir.node — STREAMING directory-tree iteration (find).
#
# The directory-source primitive: reduces `find PATH -type f|-type d
# [-maxdepth N]` and `find … | wc -l` pipelines to a lazy per-entry loop —
# the tree is walked entry-by-entry (O(depth) memory beyond the loop var),
# never materialized as a list, and file CONTENTS are never opened.
# Body statements use the existing VALUE primitives per entry. See
# docs/shir-primitives.md §WalkDir for the pinned GNU find semantics.

node WalkDir
tag "WalkDir"
field source: expr
field var: string
field body: stmts
field type_filter: optional_string
field maxdepth: optional_expr
